location":"US","published_at":"2013-07-13T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Session","position":2}},{"id":"Np6O5ZA_1xE","position":8,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam Funk - Killdat aka Killdatmuthafu*ka","track":{"id":"nrmfLSvo5oU","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/killdat-aka-killdatmuthafu-ka/","slug":"killdat-aka-killdatmuthafuka","title":"Killdat aka Killdatmuthafu*ka","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":null},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"IgJtl2M_Vk0","slug":"140","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-140-w"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #140 w/ Esta & Andres","artwork":"/images/episodes/140.jpg","content":"\nESTA and Andres stop on by and deliver solid sets.\n\n<!--more-->\n\nHad to start this show with a new unreleased gem from Kaytra and play all the classics/unreleased material as usual. Esta finally stopped by to drop an official set and talk about what's next for him. He really impressed us with his house vibes. This man is diverse. Andres also came through and graced us with a heavy hitter set. Spread this if you feel it.\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10805,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-08-10T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"Q_6ILvoMSAU","position":31,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam Funk - Killdat aka Killdatmuthafu*ka","track":{"id":"nrmfLSvo5oU","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/killdat-aka-killdatmuthafu-ka/","slug":"killdat-aka-killdatmuthafuka","title":"Killdat aka Killdatmuthafu*ka","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":null},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"UMjXwUAv27s","slug":"148","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-148"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #148","artwork":"/images/episodes/148.jpg","content":"\nContinuing Joe Kay's 24th birthday celibration with precise selections that you either forgot about or never heard.\n\n<!--more-->\n\nIn celebration of Joe's 24th birthday yesterday, we started celebrating on Thursday at The Sound of Tomorrow (The Crosby) with Astronautica & starRo! Thank you to everyone who came out and supported, what a show it was. This radio session is just a continuation of the celebration with precise selections that you either forgot about or never heard. \nBless to those who tuned into the live broadcast via Kbeach. It's amazing to think about how far we've came. \n\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10830,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-10-12T01:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"Wlg9G9yqF48","position":18,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam-Funk - Killdat a.k.a. Killdatmuthafu*ka","track":{"id":"mvb2B1N6jxI","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/killdat-a-k-a-killdatmuthafu-ka/","slug":"killdat-aka-killdatmuthafuka","title":"Killdat a.k.a. Killdatmuthafu*ka","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/killdat-a-k-a-killdatmuthafu-ka.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"liNF_Uad_x0","slug":"151","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-151-w-mr"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #151 w/ Mr. Choc (Beat Junkies)","artwork":"/images/episodes/151.jpg","content":"\nFor this week's special guest if you want to talk about pioneers in the game [Mr. Choc](https://twitter.com/MrChocFan4) is one of them. \n\n<!--more-->\n\nOne of our favorite DJ's who's talent and accomplishments are not to be overlooked. \nRepresenting the world famous Beat Junkies crew and Skam Artists, the crew was blessed to have this man come by Kbeach and hit us with a set and great interview session. \nThe thing we admire the most about Choc is that he has his ears close to the new generation of music and understands the culture. \nHe threw down a really diverse set and kept us on our toes. \n\nJoe Kay was on his soulful chop vibe and has really been digging back into the classic neo-soul/boombap sound. \nMake sure you really pay attention to the interview at the end. \nSome great insight on commercial radio on the west coast as well as opportunities for upcoming DJ's. \n\n\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10812,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-11-09T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Mr. Choc's Set","position":1}},{"id":"vtdtVRvPDrU","position":48,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam Funk - Love Is Here 2nite (I Can Feel It)","track":{"id":"lsPD0Xl-lD8","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it/","slug":"love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it","title":"Love Is Here 2nite (I Can Feel It)","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"BDetsr-_b9I","slug":"154","tags":[1,15],"links":{},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #154","artwork":"/images/episodes/154.jpg","content":"Joe Kay really displayed a crazy selection of music that will have you copying/pasting consistently within Google for some time. \n\n<!--more-->\n\nThere are a lot of new tunes sprinkled with the 'feel-good' classics that we always connect to our sets. It's essential for us to keep educating you with the influences and how it all connects to where we are today. Spread this set to as many people as possible! More minds and ears need to hear this music!\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10901,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-11-30T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"lW3szXf31kI","position":49,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam Funk - Hood Pass Intact","track":{"id":"8DX0YFEQB2M","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/hood-pass-intact/","slug":"hood-pass-intact","title":"Hood Pass Intact","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/hood-pass-intact.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"BDetsr-_b9I","slug":"154","tags":[1,15],"links":{},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #154","artwork":"/images/episodes/154.jpg","content":"Joe Kay really displayed a crazy selection of music that will have you copying/pasting consistently within Google for some time. \n\n<!--more-->\n\nThere are a lot of new tunes sprinkled with the 'feel-good' classics that we always connect to our sets. It's essential for us to keep educating you with the influences and how it all connects to where we are today. Spread this set to as many people as possible! More minds and ears need to hear this music!\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10901,"location":"US","published_at":"2013-11-30T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"-S2WWGWp4OA","position":36,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam-Funk - Brookside Park","track":{"id":"Kq8aumvHbUA","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/brookside-park/","slug":"brookside-park","title":"Brookside Park","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/brookside-park.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"brFh4QBhAJE","slug":"167","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-167"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #167","artwork":"/images/episodes/167.jpg","content":"Take a deep breath and slow things down with Joe Kay\n<!--more-->\n\nSo many good things have been going on in our world but sometimes it is overwhelming. However we just take a deep breath and keep it moving. This week Joe Kay wanted to slow things down a bit and just focus on the music by going solo. Joe started off with some nice neo-soul/Dilla-esque vibes and then progressed into some progressive beats to get your energy flowing. Standout artists to look out for are LOSCO. These guys have a heavy, heavy sound. Just wait til you hear. As the show progressed the engagement via social media was massive and a few people randomly requested to hear a Sango tribute so we did one! Joe dropped a 42 minute set of primarily unreleased music to keep things interesting! We hope you enjoy the show and feel free to spread it to as many people as possible. Real radio is here.\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10845,"location":"US","published_at":"2014-03-01T00:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Set","position":0}},{"id":"idQbiwHSGKM","position":20,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam-Funk - Fadin'","track":{"id":"tYsHAVnZqwA","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/fadin/","slug":"fadin","title":"Fadin'","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/fadin.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"MUTAwmt5Mm0","slug":"173","tags":[1,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-173"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #173","artwork":"/images/episodes/173.jpg","content":"Joe Kay makes it to the studio in time to throw down an unforgettable set full of primarily forgotten classics that will have you reminiscing on life.\n\n<!--more-->\n\nAs if this news isn't enough, we just hit 100K here on Soundcloud this past Friday literally while we launched our new residency @ the legendary Echoplex! Talk about timing and accomplishments. THANK you to each and every one of you for supporting us and spreading this sound to everyone. We plan to give you something really soon to celebrate 100K supporters worldwide and more. Big ups to the 900+ people who showed up to The Sound of Tomorrow this past Friday. Very inspiring.\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10836,"location":"US","published_at":"2014-05-03T01:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Session","position":0}},{"id":"55XG1CUwE0o","position":68,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam Funk - Love Is Here 2nite (I Can Feel It)","track":{"id":"lsPD0Xl-lD8","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it/","slug":"love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it","title":"Love Is Here 2nite (I Can Feel It)","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"eMlUtMnJUio","slug":"176","tags":[8,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-176-rinse-fm-launch"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #176 (RINSE FM Launch)","artwork":"/images/episodes/176.jpg","content":"\n<!--more-->\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","profile":"QiEFFErt688","duration":10778,"location":"US","published_at":"2014-06-21T01:00:00+00:00"},"title":"Joe Kay's Session","position":0}},{"id":"fqQEzLn59pY","position":21,"timestamp":null,"rawTrack":"Dam Funk - Love Is Here 2nite (I Can Feel It)","track":{"id":"lsPD0Xl-lD8","path":"/artists/dam-funk/tracks/love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it/","slug":"love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it","title":"Love Is Here 2nite (I Can Feel It)","artist":{"slug":"dam-funk","title":"Dam-Funk"},"artwork":"images/artists/dam-funk/tracks/love-is-here-2nite-i-can-feel-it.jpg"},"chapter":{"show":{"id":"kl47T3kNDKo","slug":"177","tags":[8,3,15],"links":{"soundcloud":"https://soundcloud.com/soulection/soulection-radio-show-177-ft-dpat-siveys-live-set"},"state":"published","title":"Soulection Radio Show #177 Ft. (Dpat + Sivey's Live Set)","artwork":"/images/epis